- [ ] Sibling redundancy with parent install service: "every read through
  initContent" is parent's chokepoint invariant; "per-file idempotency
  pattern" is parent's skip-existing rule.
  Traces to: outcomes, Strategy | Sibling-redundancy
  Misalignment: spec-gap
  Category: Sibling-redundancy

- [ ] Carry-forward (prior cycle): 2 unchecked items. Re-walk after rewrite.

## Retro

This spec restates the parent install service's contract from a slightly
different angle. The bloat-driver is treating "verbatim copy" as needing
to be enforced by 4 separate outcomes; one outcome ("docs land on disk
byte-identical to canonical") suffices.
